<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!--
    FrilModList - XUi windows

    TWO CHANGES, both into vanilla's own in-game menu file.

    1. A "Mods" button in the ESC menu's left-hand column.

       Vanilla declares that column as a plain vertical grid inside <window name="ingameMenu">,
       so the button is one more <simplebutton> in the same grid with the same depth, width,
       height and font_size as its neighbours.

       INSERTED AFTER btnTpPoi, NOT APPENDED, and that is deliberate. The last two entries in
       vanilla's list, btnOpenConsole and btnBugReport, both carry a `visible` condition, so
       appending would put ours after two buttons that are usually hidden. btnTpPoi is the last
       unconditional one.

    2. The window the button opens.

       v1.1.0: REBUILT ON VANILLA'S OWN FURNITURE. Fril: "the window is off. It needs moving
       into the centre and as its a standalone mod can we use the same format as vanilla does.
       The sandbox window is image 2 for reference." v1.0.0 was a hand-drawn green terminal
       panel borrowed from the Ostrich's register, which suits a diegetic hotel screen and does
       not suit a utility window sitting next to Options and Sandbox Options.

       Copied from <window name="sandboxOptions"> rather than approximated:

         - the same 1260x800, so the two sit identically when you flick between them
         - <headerbg /> and a label with style="header.name" for the title bar
         - a content rect at pos 0,-46 with <boxbg /> and padding 20
         - a scrollview holding three 390-wide columns at x 0, 400 and 800, font_size 28
         - vanilla's own colour convention for the text, see the controller

       THE CENTRING RULE, which is what was actually wrong. With anchor="center" the position
       is the offset to the window's TOP-LEFT corner, not to its middle. Vanilla writes
       pos="-630,400" for a 1260x800 window: minus half the width, plus half the height. Get
       that wrong and the window hangs off to one side, which is exactly what v1.0.0 did.

       v1.5.1: pause_game="true" REMOVED. The note here used to say it "matches sandboxOptions",
       and it matched the spelling and nothing else. It is NOT a window attribute: it occurs once
       in all of vanilla's XML, on that one window, and it is a custom attribute of that one
       controller. So this window never paused anything. The ESC menu pauses, opening this closed
       the menu and unpaused, and a player reading the list was stood in the world. The pause is
       now done in the controller's OnOpen and OnClose, where vanilla does it.
-->
<configs>

    <insertAfter xpath="//window[@name='ingameMenu']/grid[@name='buttons']/simplebutton[@name='btnTpPoi']">
        <simplebutton name="btnMods" depth="3" width="250" height="46" caption_key="xuiFrilMenuMods" font_size="34" />
    </insertAfter>

    <append xpath="/windows">

        <window name="windowFrilModList" anchor="center" pos="-630,400" width="1260" height="800"
                controller="FrilModList, FrilModList" cursor_area="true">

            <rect name="header" height="43" depth="1">
                <headerbg />
                <label style="header.name" pos="6,-6" width="550" text_key="xuiFrilMenuMods" />
            </rect>

            <rect name="content" pos="0,-46" height="${parentinnerheight-46}" depth="1" padding="20">
                <boxbg />

                <label name="count" depth="1" pos="0,-2" width="${parentinnerwidth-10}" height="40"
                       text="{frilmodcount}" font_size="32" color="[white]" pivot="topleft" />

                <rect name="modValues" pos="0,-55" height="${parentinnerheight-55}" depth="2"
                      on_scroll="true" gamepad_selectable="true" snap="false" use_selection_box="true">
                    <defaultscrollbar />
                    <scrollview pos="5,0" width="${parentinnerwidth-10-20}" clippingsoftness="0,10">
                        <label name="modsText1" depth="4" pos="000,0" width="390" height="400"
                               text="{frilmodcol1}" font_size="28" color="[white]"
                               pivot="topleft" overflow="resizeheight" />
                        <label name="modsText2" depth="4" pos="400,0" width="390" height="400"
                               text="{frilmodcol2}" font_size="28" color="[white]"
                               pivot="topleft" overflow="resizeheight" />
                        <label name="modsText3" depth="4" pos="800,0" width="390" height="400"
                               text="{frilmodcol3}" font_size="28" color="[white]"
                               pivot="topleft" overflow="resizeheight" />
                    </scrollview>
                </rect>
            </rect>

        </window>

    </append>

</configs>
